  "review_notes": [
    "הַנָּבִיא הַהוּא and הַחוֹלֵם הַהוּא are read under rule 41: the demonstrative pronoun takes the written *that* and both articles of each phrase go unrepresented; the construct דִּבְרֵי then takes a supplied *the* of its own.",
    "A competing reading would front the *the* of *the words* onto the article of נָבִיא under rule 29; that is rejected because the rectum is not rendered anarthrously here — a determiner stands before its own word."
  ]
